WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:06.839
To add fractions, the pieces must be the same size. Let's add one half and one third.

00:07.289 --> 00:14.240
Halves and thirds are different sizes. We need a common denominator. Six works for both,

00:14.240 --> 00:17.320
because two and three both go into six.

00:17.770 --> 00:25.781
Change each fraction to sixths. One half is three sixths, because we multiply the top and bottom by three.

00:26.231 --> 00:31.873
One third is two sixths, because we multiply the top and bottom by two.

00:32.323 --> 00:39.154
Now the pieces match, so we add the tops. Three sixths plus two sixths is five sixths.

00:39.154 --> 00:40.822
The bottom stays six.
